# Biome 1, level 19 — The Junction
#
# One spring, two hubs, and a trunk that belongs to both routes. A conduit counts in the length of
# every route that runs through it, so the two cells below the spring are paid for twice: 182 to one
# hub and 182 to the other, from five conduits rather than six.
#
# The three-way conduits are what make it possible. They are the only tile that can be the branch,
# and there are two of them in a bag of seven, so the moment one arrives decides where the fork goes.

